From: NeiroNext <mihail.rozshko@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 05:38:01 +0000
Subject: Request org.gnome.ScreenSaver first and alone decisive in a Unity
 session

In a Unity session unity-settings-daemon's screensaver proxy asks for
org.freedesktop.ScreenSaver and can get it before light-locker starts.
light-locker then stopped at start ("screensaver already running in
this session") and Unity, which asks for org.gnome.ScreenSaver later,
became the locker. The proxy forwards Lock, SetActive and GetActive on
that name to org.gnome.ScreenSaver and Inhibit to the session manager.

When XDG_CURRENT_DESKTOP lists Unity (as a whole name):
 - the check for a running screensaver at start looks at
   org.gnome.ScreenSaver only;
 - org.gnome.ScreenSaver is requested first; when light-locker does not
   become its owner (another owner, or an error from the bus) it stops
   with the error as before, before any other name is requested and
   before the locked hint is written;
 - org.freedesktop.ScreenSaver is requested next; when that fails it is
   logged at debug level and light-locker goes on, without an error;
 - the result of acquiring the names is the org.gnome.ScreenSaver one.
No name is taken from another owner. On other desktops the names are
requested as before.

The Unity check of the lock-after-screensaver change is shared as
gs_desktop_is_unity () and tested in test-lock-after.

Forwarded: no
Last-Update: 2026-10-17
